","static-analysis","static-code-analysis"],"visibility":"public","forks":1204,"open_issues":1060,"watchers":5620,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/pulls/2753","html_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/pull/2753","diff_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/pull/2753.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/pylint-dev/pylint/pull/2753.patch","merged_at":"2019-03-19T09:45:10Z"},"body":"<!--\r\n\r\nThank you for submitting a PR to pylint!\r\n\r\nTo ease the process of reviewing your PR, do make sure to complete the following boxes.\r\n\r\nYou can also read more about contributing to pylint in this document:\r\nhttps://github.com/PyCQA/pylint/blob/master/doc/development_guide/contribute.rst#repository\r\n-->\r\n\r\n## Steps\r\n\r\n- [OK ] Add a ChangeLog entry describing what your PR does.\r\n- [OK ] If it's a new feature or an important bug fix, add a What's New entry in `doc/whatsnew/<current release.rst>`.\r\n- [OK ] Write a good description on what the PR does.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nThis PR introduces a new message : ``missing-parentheses-for-call-in-test`` that checks if parentheses are missing in a function call located inside a test.\r\nIt can handle call to function, method and lambdas.\r\n@PCManticore i wonder if ``maybe_callable.infer_call_result(node)`` is correct for lambdas. I pass the node as the caller but i'm not really sure.\r\nThe message is emitted if the function is a predicate, i.e if it returns a Boolean. \r\nIt is emitted if the test is an if, or an if expression or if it is  inside comprehensions.\r\n\r\n## Type of Changes\r\n<!-- Leave the corresponding lines for the applicable type of change: -->\r\n|   | Type |\r\n| ------------- | ------------- |\r\n| ✓  | :bug: Bug fix  |\r\n| ✓  | :sparkles: New feature |\r\n\r\n\r\n## Related Issue\r\nClose #2658 \r\n<!-- \r\nIf this PR fixes a particular issue, use the following to automatically close that issue\r\nonce this PR gets merged:\r\n\r\nCloses #XXX \r\n-->\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2753/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/2753/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2212938904,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjIxMjkzODkwNA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/events/2212938904","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/448166?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore","html_url":"https://github.com/PCManticore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PCManticore/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"closed","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2019-03-19T09:45:10Z","state_reason":null,"performed_via_github_app":null},{"id":2212939016,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDIyMTI5MzkwMTY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pylint-dev/pylint/issues/events/2212939016","actor":{"login":"PCManticore","id":448166,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODE2Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.gith